                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
          %p
            is the hallmark of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#holographic_relation_to_higher_chernsimons_theory Holographic relation to higher Chern-Simons theory
          %h4#idea_and_examples Idea and examples
          %p
            Generally,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} higher dimensional Chern-Simons theory
            in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 4
                  %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4k+3
            (for
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographically
            related to self-dual higher gauge theory in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 4
                  %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4k+2
            (at least in the abelian case).
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k=0)
                \: ordinary 3-dimensional
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
                is related to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
                on its boundary;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
