                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/76393468.pdf"} pdf
            %li{:id => "MiaoMüller-Kirsten00"}
              %p
                Yan-Gang Miao and H. J. W. Müller-Kirsten,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Self-duality of various chiral boson actions
                %strong 62
                (2000) 045014 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.62.045014"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.62.045014
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p A quick exposition of the basic idea is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Distler"}> Jacques Distler
              ,
              %em Actions for self-dual gauge fields
              (
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/~distler/blog/archives/000809.html"}> blog
              )
          %p
            A precise formulation of the phenomenon in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Uncertainty of Fluxes
                %strong 271
                (2007) 247-274 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0605198"}> arXiv:hep-th/0605198
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-006-0181-3"} doi:10.1007/s00220-006-0181-3
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Heisenberg Groups and Noncommutative Fluxes
                %strong 322
                (2007) 236-285 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0605200"}> arXiv:hep-th/0605200
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aop.2006.07.014"} doi:10.1016/j.aop.2006.07.014
            %li#BBSS15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Becker"}> Christian Becker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Benini"} Marco Benini
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Schenkel"} Alexander Schenkel
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"} Richard Szabo
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Abelian duality on globally hyperbolic spacetimes
                %strong 349
                (2017) 361-392 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.00316"}> arXiv:1511.00316
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-016-2669-9"} doi:10.1007/s00220-016-2669-9
          %p
            The idea of describing self-dual higher gauge theory by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holography"} holography
            with abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} higher dimensional Chern-Simons theory
            in one dimension higher originates in
          %ul
            %li#Witten96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Five-Brane Effective Action In M-Theory
                %strong 22
                (1997) 103-133 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0393-0440(97)80160-X"}> doi:10.1016/S0393-0440(97)80160-X
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9610234"} arXiv:hep-th/9610234
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Duality Relations Among Topological Effects In String Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/2000/05/031"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/2000/05/031
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9912086"} arXiv:hep-th/9912086
          %p Conceptual aspects of this are also discussed in section 6.2 of
          %ul
            %li
              S. L. Lyakhovich,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+A.+Sharapov"} A. A. Sharapov
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantizing non-Lagrangian gauge theories: an augmentation method
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0612086"} arXiv:hep-th/0612086
          %p
            Motivated by this the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            of self-dual fields had been discussed in
          %ul
            %li#HopkinsSinger
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"}> Mike Hopkins
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quadratic+Functions+in+Geometry%2C+Topology%2C+and+M-Theory"} Quadratic Functions in Geometry, Topology, and M-Theory
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            in 6d self-dual higher gauge theory via
            = succeed "-deformation:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-commutative+geometry"} non-commutative
          %ul
