              %em
                An analogue of the space of conformal blocks in
                = succeed "-dimensions" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 4
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (4k+2)
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.kyoto-u.ac.jp/~kgomi/papers/acb.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            For the case of nonabelian self-dual 1-form gauge fields see the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+instanton"} Yang-Mills instanton
          %p
            Another proposal for a Lagrangian for self-dual higher gauge fields, at the cost of an unusual kinds of decoupled
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/auxiliary+fields"} auxiliary fields
          %ul
            %li#Sen20
